<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Interactive FAQ</title>
  <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
</head>
<body class="bg-cyan-50 font-sans p-5">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto my-5">
    <h1 class="text-center text-3xl font-bold text-cyan-700">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="text-center text-slate-500 mt-1 mb-6">Web Development Basics - click a question to see the answer</p>

    <!-- Each FAQ item = a question button + an answer box.
         The answer has the Tailwind class "hidden" (display: none) so it is hidden at first. -->
    <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow mb-3 overflow-hidden">
      <button class="faq-question w-full flex justify-between items-center text-left px-5 py-4 font-bold text-teal-900 hover:bg-cyan-100">
        What is HTML? <span class="icon text-2xl text-cyan-700">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">HTML (HyperText Markup Language) is the standard language used to create the structure of a web page using tags such as headings, paragraphs, images and links.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow mb-3 overflow-hidden">
      <button class="faq-question w-full flex justify-between items-center text-left px-5 py-4 font-bold text-teal-900 hover:bg-cyan-100">
        What is CSS used for? <span class="icon text-2xl text-cyan-700">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) is used to style web pages. It controls colours, fonts, spacing and layout.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow mb-3 overflow-hidden">
      <button class="faq-question w-full flex justify-between items-center text-left px-5 py-4 font-bold text-teal-900 hover:bg-cyan-100">
        What is JavaScript? <span class="icon text-2xl text-cyan-700">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">JavaScript is a programming language that makes web pages interactive, for example handling button clicks, validating forms and updating content without reloading.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow mb-3 overflow-hidden">
      <button class="faq-question w-full flex justify-between items-center text-left px-5 py-4 font-bold text-teal-900 hover:bg-cyan-100">
        What is Tailwind CSS? <span class="icon text-2xl text-cyan-700">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">Tailwind CSS is a utility-first CSS framework. Instead of writing separate CSS, we apply small ready-made classes like <b>p-4</b> or <b>text-center</b> directly in the HTML.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow mb-3 overflow-hidden">
      <button class="faq-question w-full flex justify-between items-center text-left px-5 py-4 font-bold text-teal-900 hover:bg-cyan-100">
        What is the DOM? <span class="icon text-2xl text-cyan-700">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">The DOM (Document Object Model) represents the web page as a tree of objects. JavaScript uses it to read and change the elements of the page.</div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-center text-sm text-slate-600 mt-6">Parul Wanjari - CD25029</p>
  </div>

  <script>
    // Select all question buttons
    const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".faq-question");

    // Add a click event listener to every question
    questions.forEach(function (question) {
      question.addEventListener("click", function () {
        const answer = question.nextElementSibling;   // the answer box right after the button
        const icon = question.querySelector(".icon"); // the + / - sign

        // toggle() removes the class "hidden" if present, adds it if missing
        answer.classList.toggle("hidden");

        // Is the answer visible now?
        const isOpen = !answer.classList.contains("hidden");

        // Change the icon and highlight the open question
        icon.textContent = isOpen ? "-" : "+";
        question.classList.toggle("bg-cyan-100", isOpen);
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
